Thanks a lot everyone.  This has been very informative.  So taking
everyone's advice into account, here's my plan ...

I agree that late game Identify is not as critical as it is in the
early/mid game.  My principal reason for wanting it is to be able to
determine how many charges I have in my various wands (teleport, and
death mostly) and what my weapon enchantments are.  All in all, I'll
probably be wanting to ID between 40 and 50 items (quite a few rings
left).  So it'd be a big convenience and would save me from having to
use magic marker charges since I'll probably need those for other
scrolls.  Polypiling is also going to be somewhat limited (only one
wand of polymorph so far) so acquiring heaps of magic markers won't be
as easy as it was for my last game as an archeologist.  So, from the
spell calculator (thanks!) I will plan on finding a robe and bringing
my Int up to 16 (yes, I'm an orc) and then from XL 20 - 25 my failure
rate for Identify decreases from 74% to 20%.  Not bad, especially since
I will not be casting in the heat of battle.  I'll just keep a robe in
my bag for when I need it.

I think that bringing a helm of brilliance, and the rest of my gear, up
to full strength would just take too much effort.  _If_ I find a helm
of brilliance and have extra enchant armor scrolls then I'll use it,
but otherwise I'll go for a helm of telepathy.  For spellcasting, I
will just go for the robe, which will be acquired (hopefully) from a
certain priest of Moloch, courtesy of some polymorphed pets.  Finding
the spellbook is another matter.

As for create monster, I just wanted that to speed up my altar camping
but with a ring of slow digestion, I just stand on a burned Elbereth
and search "n10s".  Boring, yes, but it's working out satisfactorily.

Thanks again everyone. Only 9 b!oGA, b!oE, and/or mind flayer corpses
to go!
